[3.687,"o","note: recorded this stack's infrastructure in openvidu-stack.yml, so the command that continues this deploy needs no flags\r\n"]
[4.799,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nRun these commands yourself in your Azure subscription (location northeurope); ov runs none of them.\r\nOnce they have finished, run this same command again: ov finds the machines and ends the deploy.\r\n\r\n  # SSH access: the key pair for this stack, its public half handed to the template.\r\n  #   .openvidu/azure/ov-e2ec-s125357-key.pub\r\n  # The template, rendered from the one embedded in this CLI for the single node topology,\r\n  # written out for you to read (az compiles the Bicep itself):\r\n  #   .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-singlenode.bicep\r\n  az group create --name ov-e2ec-s125357-rg --location northeurope --tags created-by=openvidu-cli --only-show-errors -o none\r\n  # Create the machine. deployedBy=instance: it installs OpenVidu on itself with the\r\n  # OpenVidu CLI. The command returns when Azure is done (about 4 minutes); OpenVidu comes up after.\r\n  az deployment group create --resource-group ov-e2ec-s125357-rg --name ov-e2ec-s125357 --template-file .openvidu/azure/cf-openvidu-singlenode.bicep --only-show-errors --query properties.provisioningState -o tsv --parameters certificateType=selfsigned deployedBy=instance registryStorage=false stackName=ov-e2ec-s125357 'publicIpAddressObject={\"newOrExistingOrNone\":\"new\",\"name\":\"ov-e2ec-s125357-pip\"}' adminSshKey=\"{\\\"sshPublicKey\\\":\\\"$(cat .openvidu/azure/ov-e2ec-s125357-key.pub)\\\"}\"\r\n\r\n  # What the stack published: URL and credentials, as secrets in the Key Vault the deployment outputs (OPENVIDU_URL appears once\r\n  # OpenVidu serves: until then this read fails, and ov waits for it).\r\n  az deployment group show --resource-group ov-e2ec-s125357-rg --name ov-e2ec-s125357 --query properties.outputs -o json\r\n  KV=\"$(az deployment group show --resource-group ov-e2ec-s125357-rg --name ov-e2ec-s125357 --query properties.outputs.sharedInfoKeyVault.value -o tsv)\"\r\n  az keyvault secret show --vault-name $KV --name OPENVIDU-URL --query value -o tsv\r\n\r\nNothing above has been run. Once these commands have finished, run this same command again:\r\n\r\n  ov stack deploy ov-e2ec-s125357 --cloud azure --mode assisted\r\n\r\nIt finds the machines, waits for OpenVidu to come up and registers this directory as the\r\nstack. It creates nothing in your account.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
